@startuml
title MBSE Use Cases - Advanced Movement Tasks

left to right direction
skinparam shadowing false

actor "Mission Operator" as Operator
actor "Simulation Clock" as Clock
actor "Legacy Scenario File" as Legacy

rectangle "Advanced Movement Task Capability" {
  usecase "Assign Follow Entity" as UC_FollowEntity
  usecase "Assign Intercept Entity" as UC_Intercept
  usecase "Assign Follow Route" as UC_FollowRoute
  usecase "Build Route With\nWaypoint Altitudes" as UC_BuildRoute
  usecase "Execute Plan Steps" as UC_ExecutePlan
  usecase "Advance To Next Step" as UC_Advance
  usecase "Report Operational Status" as UC_Status
  usecase "Load Legacy Plans\nand Scenarios" as UC_Legacy
  usecase "Persist Scenario" as UC_Persist

  usecase "Maintain Follow Distance" as UC_MaintainDistance
  usecase "Intercept In 3D" as UC_Intercept3D
  usecase "Navigate Ordered Waypoints" as UC_NavigateRoute
  usecase "Handle Target Unavailable" as UC_TargetUnavailable
  usecase "Handle Timeout" as UC_Timeout
  usecase "Detect Safe Route Overshoot" as UC_Overshoot
}

Operator --> UC_FollowEntity
Operator --> UC_Intercept
Operator --> UC_FollowRoute
Operator --> UC_BuildRoute
Operator --> UC_ExecutePlan
Operator --> UC_Status

Clock --> UC_ExecutePlan
Clock --> UC_MaintainDistance
Clock --> UC_Intercept3D
Clock --> UC_NavigateRoute

Legacy --> UC_Legacy
Operator --> UC_Persist

UC_FollowEntity .> UC_MaintainDistance : <<include>>
UC_Intercept .> UC_Intercept3D : <<include>>
UC_FollowRoute .> UC_NavigateRoute : <<include>>
UC_FollowRoute .> UC_Overshoot : <<include>>
UC_ExecutePlan .> UC_Advance : <<include>>
UC_ExecutePlan .> UC_TargetUnavailable : <<extend>>
UC_ExecutePlan .> UC_Timeout : <<extend>>
UC_Legacy .> UC_Intercept : <<include>>
UC_Legacy .> UC_FollowRoute : <<include>>

note right of UC_Intercept
Visible user task:
"Intercept Entity"

No 2D/3D option in UI.
Runtime behavior is 3D.
end note

note bottom of UC_BuildRoute
Air waypoint altitude is editable.
Ground route altitude is 0 m for now.
Legacy missing altitude does not force Air to 0.
end note

@enduml
